{
  "summary": "Rejects node startup with an error when -port=65535 and an automatic Tor onion service port needs to be derived. It prevents port 65535 from wrapping around to 0 when adding 1 for the onion bind port. Configurations using an explicit onion bind port or -listen=0 remain permitted, and test coverage is added to feature_port.py.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core calculates the default Tor onion service bind port as -port + 1. When -port is set to 65535, integer wrapping results in port 0, causing the node to bind 127.0.0.1 to an arbitrary OS-assigned ephemeral port for its automatic onion service rather than failing gracefully.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The default onion bind uses -port + 1. With -port=65535 this wraps to 0, so the node binds 127.0.0.1 to a random port and the automatic onion service points there.'"
  ],
